<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ravi Varma Kulasekhara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1299–1314</span> · Also known as Ravivarman Kulasekhara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ravi">Ravi</a> Varma Kulasekhara was a king of Venad in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kollam">Kollam</a> from 1299 to 1314. Taking advantage of the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> kingdom after the raids of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, he campaigned across southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>. He was a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> literature, and his conquests did not outlast him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ravi-varma-kulasekhara.jpg" alt="Ravi Varma Kulasekhara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joachim Specht · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kollam_%C3%9Cbersicht.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
